.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-step-check 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-step\-check \- Say hit or miss for a step\*(Aqs inputs, arguments and tools, and remember the key a record must match
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten step check\fR [\fB\-\-arg\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIstep\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Say hit or miss for a step\*(Aqs inputs, arguments and tools, and remember the key a record must match
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-arg\fR \fI<arg>\fR
A value the step\*(Aqs verdict depends on beyond its inputs, keyed in order (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIstep\fR>
The step\*(Aqs name, as the consumer\*(Aqs step table declares it
